rance sum -- two successive claims\");\n    it.todo(\"should round payout down in MHPCO's favor -- 350.5 G -> 350 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim for unknown item type in damages -- non-zero exit\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim for negative damage amount -- non-zero exit\");\n  });\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784923139186},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-41-05_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-41-05_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (30 tests | 27 skipped) 2ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  3 passed | 27 todo (30)\n   Start at  19:58:59\n   Duration  155ms (transform 23ms, setup 0ms, collect 22ms, tests 2ms, environment 0ms, prepare 48ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784923139186},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We have implementation quote returns base fee for empty list, sword premium for sword, component premium per rune. We need to refactor while tests green. Let's assess naming: quote for customer/items returns number. Maybe quote is fine. But the function currently manually checks items[0].type, and uses filter. Could extract functions: isSword, countRunes, etc. But Rule 2 clarity. Also claim returns undefined. It is unused by tests but exported. Could leave. But quote has duplication: BASE_FEE appears twice; componentCount conditional. Could refactor to compute premium and add base fee once. Mass calculation before. Also naming evaluation: function name `quote` maybe okay. Variables: items, customer, policy, incident. Let's think about upcoming spec: runes block discount, cursed surcharge, enchantments, loyalty, contract status, rounding. The current code is minima