item.type === type).length;\n\nexport const quote = (customer: Customer, insuredItems: Item[]): number => {\n  if (insuredItems.length > 0 && insuredItems[0].type === \"sword\") {\n    return BASE_FEE + SWORD_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  const runeCount = countByType(insuredItems, \"rune\");\n  if (runeCount === COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK) {\n    return BASE_FEE + COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  const moonstoneCount = countByType(insuredItems, \"moonstone\");\n  const componentCount = runeCount + moonstoneCount;\n  return BASE_FEE + componentCount * COMPONENT_PREMIUM;\n};\n\nexport const claim = (policy: any, incident: any): any => {\n  return undefined;\n};\n```\n\nComponent count:\n\n- Constants: 9 → 9\n- Bindings: 18 → 18\n- Invocations: 8 (`filter`, `countByType` ×2, `+` ×4, `*` ×1) → 16\n- Conditionals: 2 → 8\n- Loops: 2 → 10\n- Assignments: 0 → 0\n\n**Total Mass: 61**\n\n**Mass Change: 65 → 61 (−4)**\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n1. **Naming / Intent**\n   - `RUNE_PREMIUM` → `COMPONENT_PREMIUM`\n   - `RUNE_BLOCK_PREMIUM` → `COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM`\n   - Extracted `COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK = 3` to name the block-size rule.\n   - Added `Item` and `Customer` types, removing `any` from `quote`.\n\n2. **No Duplication (DRY)**\n   - Replaced `countRunes` + `countMoonstones` with a single `countByType` helper.\n   - Consolidated the rune/moonstone premium calculation into `componentCount * COMPONENT_PREMIUM`.\n\n3. **Fewer Elements / Simpler Expression**\n   - The final premium expression now adds the fee once instead of duplicating the per-type multiplication.\n\n## Simple Design Rules Check\n\n- **Rule 1 — Tests Pass:** `pnpm test` → 7 passing, 23 todo.\n- **Rule 2 — Reveals Intent:** Names now match the domain (components, blocks, component count).\n- **Rule 3 — No Duplication:** Counting logic and premium-per-component logic are no longer duplicated.\n- **Rule 4 — Fewest Elements:** Removed two helper functions and one redundant multiplication/addition pair; mass decreased.\n\n## Ver