c rates/thresholds have a single source of truth; `hasInsuranceContract` is reused.\n4. **Fewest elements:** ✅ Removed the mutable `rate` accumulator and declined an unnecessary one-off abstraction.\n\n## Note\n\nDuring the refactor an intermediate change accidentally narrowed the contract surcharge to index `0` only. The test suite caught it immediately; the final version preserves the original semantics: a surcharge applies whenever `contractIndex !== null`, and the follow-up discount stacks on top of that for indices `> 0`.\n\nTests: **all green**."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-41-05_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 11\nRecent Green phase: Added high-enchantment surcharge and made first insurance apply per quote\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 11\nRecent Green phase: Added high-enchantment surcharge and made first insurance apply per quote\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784923873117},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need respond as coding assistant refactor agent. We are told to refactor implementation while keeping all tests green. We have test file src/claim-office.spec.ts and implementation src/claim-office.ts. Passing tests 11. Need follow refactoring process: read files, calculate APP mass, evaluate naming first, apply simple design rules, implement refactoring, run tests, calculate new mass, document. Must use tools. Need likely run pnpm test. Need read source files. Also check project. Let's start.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.ls:2","name":"ls","arguments":{"path":"."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":85,"output":152,"cacheRead":5568,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":101,"totalTokens":5805,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784923873137,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-0e768f3b-f8fc-49ff-82f7-71211ecb8d8a","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"type Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n};\n\ntype Customer = {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n};\n\nconst CENTS_PER_GOLD = 100;\n\nconst BASE_FEE = 5;\nconst SWORD_PREMIUM = 100;\nconst AMULET_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK = 3;\n\nconst countByType = (items: Item[], type: string): number =>\n  items.filter((item) => item.type === type).length;\n\nconst premiumForComponentCount = (count: number): number => {\n  if (count === COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return count * COMPONENT_PREMIUM;\n};\n\nconst premiumForComponentsOfType = (items: Item[], type: string): number =>\n  premiumForComponentCount(countByType(items, type));\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (item: Item): number => {\n  if (item.type === \"sword\") return SWORD_PREMIUM;\n  if (item.type === \"amulet\") return AMULET_PREMIUM;\n  return 0;\n};\n\nconst usesEquipmentPricing = (items: Item[]): boolean =>\n  items.length > 0 && (items[0].type === \"sword\" || items[0].type === \"amulet\");\n\nconst sumBy = <T>(items: T[], valueFor: (item: T) => number): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + valueFor(item), 0);\n\nconst itemModifierCents = (item: Item): number => {\n  let modifier = 0;\n  const base = basePremiumFor(item);\n  if (item.cursed) {\n    modifier += base * 0.5;\n  }\n  if (item.enchantment !== undefined && item.enchantment >= 5) {\n    modifier += base * 0.3;\n  }\n  return modifier * CENTS_PER_GOLD;\n};\n\nconst roundUpCentsToGold = (cents: number): number =>\n  Math.ceil(cents / CENTS_PER_GOLD);\n\nconst policyModifierRate = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  contractIndex: number | null,\n): number => {\n  let rate = 0;\n  if (customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2) {\n    rate -= 0.2;\n  }\n  if (contractIndex !== null) {\n    rate += 0.1;\n  }\n  if (contractIndex !== null && contractIndex > 0) {\n    rate -= 0.15;\n  }\n  return rate;\n};\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  insuredItems: Item[],\n  contractIndex: number | null = null,\n): number => {\n  if (usesEquipmentPricing(insuredItems)) {\n    const baseCents = sumBy(\n      insuredItems,\n      (item) => basePremiumFor(item) * CENTS_PER_GOLD,\n    );\n    const itemModifierTotal = sumBy(insuredItems, itemModifierCents);\n    const policyRate = policyModifierRate(customer, contractIndex);\n    const policyModifierCents = baseCents * policyRate;\n    const totalCents =\n      baseCents + itemModifierTotal + policyModifierCents + BASE_FEE * CENTS_PER_GOLD;\n    return roundUpCentsToGold(totalCents);\n  }\n  return (\n    BASE_FEE +\n    premiumForComponentsOfType(insuredItems, \"rune\") +\n    premiumForComponentsOfType(insuredItems, \"moonstone\")\n  );\n};\n\nexport const claim = (policy: any, incident: any): any => {\n  return undefined;\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784923874796},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote, claim } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  describe(\"quote\", () => {\n    it(\"should return 5 G for empty item list -- edge case\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items: any[] = [];\n      expect(quote(customer, items)).toBe(5);\n    });\n    it(\"should return 105 G for a single plain sword -- base premium + fee\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\" }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items)).toBe(105);\n    });\n    it(\"should return 55 G for 2 runes -- 50 base premium + 5 fee\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items)).toBe(55);\n    });\n    it(\"should return 65 G for 3 runes -- 60 block premium + 5 fee\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items)).toBe(65);\n    });\n    it(\"should return 105 G for 4 runes -- 100 base + 5 fee, no block\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items)).toBe(105);\n    });\n    it(\"should return 180 G for 7 runes -- 175 base + 5 fee (two blocks + one extra)\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" });\n      expect(quote(customer, items)).toBe(180);\n    });\n    it(\"should return 80 G for 2 runes + 1 moonstone -- 75 base + 5 fee, different types no block\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items)).toBe(80);\n    });\n    it(\"should return 125 G for 3 runes + 3 moonstones -- 120 base + 5 fee (two blocks)\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items)).toBe(125);\n    });\n    it(\"should apply cursed surcharge to affected item only -- cursed sword + plain amulet -> 231 G total with first insurance\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true },\n        { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(231);\n    });\n    it(\"should return 165 G for newcomer with a cursed sword -- integration example\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(165);\n    });\n    it(\"should return 160 G for long-standing customer's second contract cursed enchanted sword -- integration example\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 7, cursed: true },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 1)).toBe(160);\n    });\n    it.todo(\"should apply high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment >= 5\");\n    it.todo(\"should not apply high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment 4\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount for customer with >= 2 years\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply first insurance surcharge for first contract\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply follow-up contract discount after first contract\");\n    it.todo(\"should round premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 197.5 G -> 198 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should exit with non-zero status for unknown item type in quote\");\n  });\n\n  describe(\"claim\", () => {\n    it.todo(\"should pay out 400 G for regular steel sword enchantment 3 damage 500 G -- standard reimbursement\");\n    it.todo(\"should pay out 100 G for rune damage 200 G -- standard reimbursement\");\n    it.todo(\"should pay out 400 G for dragon-material sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 G -- 50% rule wins over dragon\");\n    it.todo(\"should pay out 700 G for dragon-material sword enchantment 5 damage 800 G -- only dragon clause applies\");\n    it.todo(\"should pay out 400 G for steel sword enchantment 9 damage 1000 G -- only high-enchantment clause applies\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply 100 G deductible per damaged item -- dragon attack on sword and amulet -> 600 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should treat multiple damages of same type as separate events with separate deductibles\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim when damages exceed insured count of same type -- non-zero exit\");\n    it.todo(\"should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum -- two successive claims\");\n    it.todo(\"should round payout down in MHPCO's favor -- 350.5 G -> 350 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim for unknown item type in damages -- non-zero exit\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim for negative damage amount -- non-zero exit\");\n  });\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784923874796},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.ls:2","toolName":"ls","content":[{"type":"text","text":".pi/\nAGENTS.md\neslint.config.mjs\nmetrics.json\nnode_modules/\npackage.json\npnpm-lock.yaml\nprompt.md\nrun.log\nsrc/\ntsconfig.json\nvitest.config.ts"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784923874796},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need to refactor src/claim-office.ts. Tests: 11 passing; there are todos. Implementation has quote and claim stub. Need keep all tests green. We must attempt at least one