onstruct a scenario that yields 197.5.\n\nLet me think: components with block discounts. 7 runes = 175 base. With contractIndex=1: first insurance +10% = 17.5, follow-up -15% = -26.25. Net policy adjustment = -8.75. So adjusted base = 175 - 8.75 = 166.25. + fee 5 = 171.25. Ceil = 172. Not 197.5.\n\nWhat about a cursed amulet with contractIndex=1? Base=60, curse=30, first insurance=6, follow-up=-9. Adjusted base = 60 - 3 = 57. + item modifiers 30 = 87. + fee 5 = 92. Not 197.5.\n\nHmm, let me just construct a case. I want total before rounding = 197.5. Then with fee 5, base+policy+item = 192.5.\n\nMaybe a cursed staff? Staff premium is 80. Curse=40. First insurance=8. Follow-up=-12. Adjusted base = 80 - 4 = 76. + item 40 = 116. Not enough.\n\nWhat about 2 swords? base=200. With no modifiers: 200 + 5 = 205. With contractIndex=1: 200 - 10 + 5 = 195. Not 197.5.\n\nWhat about 2 swords and contractIndex=0? 200 + 20 + 5 = 225.\n\nWhat about a cursed sword (150 base item) with high enchantment (30) = 180 item premium, plus base 100, first insurance 10, fee 5 = 295.\n\nI need to find a combination that gives exactly 197.5 total. Let me think differently. The total is: base + itemSurcharges + policyAdjustment + fee.\n\nI want base + itemSurcharges + policyAdjustment = 192.5 (so +5 = 197.5).\n\nLet me try: cursed sword with contractIndex=1.\n- base = 100\n- item surcharge = 50\n- policy adjustment = 100 * (0.1 - 0.15) = -5\n- subtotal before fee = 100 + 50 - 5 = 145\n- total = 150. Not 197.5.\n\nWhat about sword + amulet with high enchantment on amulet? Amulet enchantment? The spec says items have enchantment, so amulet can have enchantment too.\n\nbase = 100 + 60 = 160.\nHigh enchantment on amulet: 60 * 0.3 = 18.\nFirst insurance: 16.\nFollow-up: -24.\ncontractIndex=1: policy adjustment = -8.\nsubtotal = 160 + 18 - 8 = 170. + fee 5 = 175.\n\nWhat about cursed sword + cursed amulet, contractIndex=1?\n- base = 160\n- item surcharge = 50 + 30 = 80\n- policy adjustment = 160 * (-0.05) = -8\n- subtotal = 160 + 80 - 8 = 232\n- total = 237.\n\nI want 192.5 before fee. Let me set up equations.\n\nLet base = B, item surcharge = S, policy rate = r. B + S + B*r = 192.5.\n\nFor contractIndex=1, r = -0.05 (first insurance +0.1, follow-up -0.15).\nSo B * 0.95 + S = 192.5.\n\nIf S = 0: B = 202.63... not integer base.\nIf S = 0.5 * b_cursed where b_cursed is part of B. Let B = b1 + b2, S = 0.5*b1 (cursed item). Then 0.95*(b1+b2) + 0.5*b1 = 192.5. 1.45*b1 + 0.95*b2 = 192.5.\n\nTry b1 = 100 (sword cursed), then 145 + 0.95*b2 = 192.5 => 0.95*b2 = 47.5 => b2 = 50. Not a valid base premium.\n\nTry b1 = 60 (amulet cursed), 87 + 0.95*b2 = 192.5 => 0.95*b2 = 105.5 => b2 = 111.05. Not valid.\n\nTry with high enchantment: S = 0.5*b1 + 0.3*b1 = 0.8*b1 (same item cursed and high enchantment). Then 0.95*(b1+b2) + 0.8*b1 = 192.5 => 1.75*b1 + 0.95*b2 = 192.5. Try b1=100: 175 + 0.95*b2 = 192.5 => b2=18.42. No.\n\nTry contractIndex=0 (r=0.1): B*1.1 + S = 192.5. If S=0, B=175. Not a base premium. If S=50 (cursed sword), 1.1*B = 142.5 => B=129.54. No.\n\nHmm, maybe I need to use components. Component base premiums are multiples of 25 or block of 60. Let me try 7 runes with contractIndex=0: B=175, S=0, r=0.1 => 175*1.1 + 5 = 197.5. Yes! 175 + 17.5 + 5 = 197.5.\n\nSo 7 runes with contractIndex=0 gives 197.5 total -> ceil 198.\n\nBut wait, runes are components and currently quote routes based on first item being sword/amulet. If first item is rune, it goes to component pricing. I need to make components also get policy modifiers and fee.\n\nActually, the spec says components are items too and should get all modifiers. The quote function should handle components the same way as equipment.\n\nI need to unify the quote logic so components also get policy modifiers. But for now, let me just write the test with 7 runes and see it fail. Then I'll fix the routing.\n\nActually, let me update the test to use 7 runes with contractIndex=0, expecting 198.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning