"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784924110672,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ec0f5e29-6604-4c8e-acc8-76f53c7c55b6","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:96","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring complete. All 17 active tests remain green (`pnpm test`).\n\n## Naming Evaluation\n\n| Name | Purpose | Assessment | Decision |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `basePremiumFor` | Map an item type to its equipment base premium | Too generic; does not say it is per-item or equipment-only | Rename to `basePremiumForItem` |\n| `itemBasePremium` | Return per-item base premium, but forces components to `0` | Misleading—components have a separate block premium | Remove; let `basePremiumForItem` return `0` for non-equipment |\n| `itemSurchargeCents` | Compute cursed/high-enchantment surcharge in cents | Acceptable, but `surchargeCentsFor(item)` reads more naturally | Rename to `surchargeCentsFor` |\n\n## Simple Design Rule Evaluation\n\n1. **Tests Pass** — `pnpm test` passes before and after refactoring.\n2. **Reveals Intent** — Added `EQUIPMENT_BASE_PREMIUMS` lookup so the equipment-to-premium mapping is explicit. `surchargeCentsFor` now uses explaining variables (`cursedSurcharge`, `enchantedSurcharge`) instead of a mutating accumulator.\n3. **No Duplication** — Removed the parallel `if` chain in `basePremiumFor` in favor of a single lookup table. Removed `itemBasePremium`, which duplicated the “component types get no individual base premium” concept.\n4. **Fewest Elements** — Eliminated one helper function and two mutable `+=` assignments.\n\n## APP Mass Calculation\n\nMass formula: `constants×1 + bindings×1 + invocations×2 + conditionals×4 + loops×5 + assignments×6`\n\n### Before refactoring\n\n| Component | Count | Mass |\n|---|---|---|\n| Constants | 36 | 36 |\n| Bindings | 66 | 66 |\n| Invocations | 18 | 36 |\n| Conditionals | 11 | 44 |\n| Loops | 2 | 10 |\n| Assignments | 2 | 12 |\n| **Total** | | 