le errors (exit non-zero and write to stderr).\n\nLet me create src/cli.ts. Then I should run tests to make sure everything still passes. Then write experiment-done.txt.\n\nActually, since the test list is complete, I can add CLI tests if needed, but the test list phase didn't include CLI tests. The spec says test files are expected, and I have src/claim-office.spec.ts. The CLI entry point is also expected.\n\nLet me create src/cli.ts.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Green -- Test 30: added negative damage amount validation\n\nGreen Phase Complete:\n**Implementation**: Added validation to throw when damage amount is negative\n**Result**: All tests now pass (30 passing)\n**Approach**: Check each damage amount in validateClaim\n\nAll tests in the test list are now implemented and passing. Proceeding to create the required CLI entry point."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.write:154","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"src/cli.ts","content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\nimport { quote, claim } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\nconst readStdin = (): Promise<string> =>\n  new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    let data = \"\";\n    process.stdin.setEncoding(\"utf8\");\n    process.stdin.on(\"data\", (chunk) => {\n      data += chunk;\n    });\n    process.stdin.on(\"end\", () => resolve(data));\n    process.stdin.on(\"error\", reject);\n  });\n\nconst run = async () => {\n  const input = await readStdin();\n  let scenario: any;\n  try {\n    scenario = JSON.parse(input);\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Invalid JSON input\");\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  const results: any[] = [];\n  const policies: { items: any[]; cap: number; remainingCap: number }[] = [];\n\n  for (let stepIndex = 0; stepIndex < scenario.steps.length; stepIndex++) {\n    const step = scenario.steps[stepIndex];\n    try {\n      if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n        const contractIndex = policies.length;\n        const premium = quote(\n          scenario.customer,\n          step.items,\n          contractIndex,\n        );\n        const insuranceSum = step.items.reduce(\n          (sum: number, item: any) => sum + getInsuranceValue(item),\n          0,\n        );\n        policies.push({\n          items: step.items,\n          cap: insuranceSum * 2,\n          remainingCap: insuranceSum * 2,\n        });\n        results.push({ premium });\n      } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n        const policy = policies[step.policy];\n        if (!policy) {\n          throw new Error(`Policy ${step.policy} not found`);\n        }\n        const result = claim(policy, step.incident);\n        policy.remainingCap = result.remainingCap;\n        results.push(result);\n      } else {\n        throw new Error(`Unknown operation: ${step.op}`);\n      }\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(\n        error instanceof Error ? error.message : \"Unknown error\",\n      );\n      process.exit(1);\n    }\n  }\n\n  console.log(JSON.stringify({ results }));\n};\n\nconst getInsuranceValue = (item: any): number => {\n  const values: Record<string, number> = {\n    sword: 1000,\n    amulet: 600,\n    staff: 800,\n    potion: 400,\n    rune: 250,\n    moonstone: 250,\n  };\n  if (!(item.type in values)) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n  }\n  return values[item.type];\n};\n\nrun();\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":224,"output":1017,"cacheRead":93504,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":262,"totalTokens":94745,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784925136657,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-61a736f6-fdc2-4070-bf4e-e9e01691b5a7","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.write:154","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 2265 bytes to src/cli.ts"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784925144556},{"role":"assistant","